  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Gradients can't be deserialized in VRC, so you can't use them to set colour transitions in the inspector. Odin does not have the UnityEngine.GradientColorKey[] and UnityEngine.GradientAlphaKey[] types generated for its AOT serializers. \nIf you try to serialize a gradient you will get the following errors when loading the world in VRC:\n```\nCreating a serialization formatter for the type 'UnityEngine.GradientAlphaKey[]' failed due to missing AOT support. \n Please use Odin's AOT generation feature to generate an AOT dll before building, and MAKE SURE that all of the following types were automatically added to the supported types list after a scan (if they were not, please REPORT AN ISSUE with the details of which exact types the scan is missing and ADD THEM MANUALLY): \nUnityEngine.GradientAlphaKey[] (name string: 'UnityEngine.GradientAlphaKey[], UnityEngine.CoreModule')\nCreating a serialization formatter for the type 'UnityEngine.GradientColorKey[]' failed due to missing AOT support. \n Please use Odin's AOT generation feature to generate an AOT dll before building, and MAKE SURE that all of the following types were automatically added to the supported types list after a scan (if they were not, please REPORT AN ISSUE with the details of which exact types the scan is missing and ADD THEM MANUALLY): \nUnityEngine.GradientColorKey[] (name string: 'UnityEngine.GradientColorKey[], UnityEngine.CoreModule')\n```\nSample script (for U#): https://gist.github.com/s-ilent/3f304b3e98889ebae531ff3d4d4ef879",
  "error": null,
